I tell Amit, Neha, and Sanjay about my first day.
"That day in January, the taxi stopped outside my building," I say.
"I picked up my heavy bags."
"I went inside the building and reached my flat."
"I was very tired."
"Just then the neighbour's door opened."
"A woman came outside."
"She looked at me and smiled."
"She asked, are you the new neighbour?"
"I said, yes, my name is Maya."
"She said, I am Asha, welcome to Mumbai."
"Then she gave me a glass of water."
"I drank the water and I felt very happy."
The three friends listen to my story and smile.
"Asha ji is very nice," Neha says.
"Your first friend is very helpful," Amit says.
"Yes," I say.
"She helped me a lot from the very first day."
